      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Papa Okafor's dairy barn. The milk truck stopped coming in the first week, and he poured forty gallons a day into the ditch until the herd began to go missing from the north stalls with the gates still latched. Something had been living in the hayloft since the Cordon closed: a drifter who climbed down at night through the boards behind the workshop and back up the tack-room ladder, where nothing that was once a cow could follow. Papa set his biggest trap in the aisle, locked the tack room, hung the key over the feed bins for Ife and went up with the shotgun. Two shots. The drifter's camp is still up there, and so is the drifter.",
